ajority?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East: Israeli strikes kill several in Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a6515de49ce53f209d818e09046b9f8f88ef3b602eebdb81770a28e29e44942</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:27Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T09:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/middle-east-israeli-strikes-kill-several-in-lebanon/live-79133242--30392cf8ce7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/middle-east-israeli-strikes-kill-several-in-lebanon/live-79133242?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lebanon's Health Ministry said at least 10 were killed in overnight Israeli strikes in the south of the country. Meanwhile, traffic in the Strait of Hormuz has sunk to its lowest level since May. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says war looks set to go on into winter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:057b215b1615dca06a542a17dae0ebce6681dff26aa06cdea5c099c1ca54a8e8</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-war-looks-set-to-go-on-into-winter/live-79135930--33643c7a4b0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-war-looks-set-to-go-on-into-winter/live-79135930?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy says there appears to be no end in sight in Russia's war against his country. His words come after another round of US-led diplomacy. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK government condemns 'thuggish' anti-migrant protests in Portsmouth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b30fff3eea44a4bd47ead12f4e340d8d027ca0df70c46f88dcfde5729ca7a9bf</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T08:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-government-condemns-thuggish-anti-migrant-protests-in-portsmouth/a-79134048--212251740773.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-government-condemns-thuggish-anti-migrant-protests-in-portsmouth/a-79134048?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds gathered in Portsmouth after some refugees arrived by boat from France, a day after masked protesters disrupted traffic at the port of Dover.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rescue efforts underway in deadly Delhi building collapse</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34401f25c8dee1ba56b4b453b2d41582514dc6dc1cdc7b5beb4e71a6054ae318</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T07:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rescue-efforts-underway-in-deadly-delhi-building-collapse/live-79123607--5263e9e58a28.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rescue-efforts-underway-in-deadly-delhi-building-collapse/live-79123607?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The building was located in New Delhi's Satya Niketan, popular among students from nearby colleges and universities. At least 12 people have been rescued from the rubble. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Jamaica to petition King Charles over slavery reparations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4793f0e4e888867c110f4156528ed80ad856197aa1e26fbdc038a3f6a539556c</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/jamaica-to-petition-king-charles-over-slavery-reparations/a-79123536--34efcede7988.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/jamaica-to-petition-king-charles-over-slavery-reparations/a-79123536?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jamaica will ask King Charles III to refer questions about the legality of slavery and Britain's potential obligation to provide reparations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Amazon cargo plane crash in Miami</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7718cfa192930b208f588794dc638a604e9dddc83f42ceeedcb5d9fff1f0e2b2</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T23:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365--4869fc3bcedd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/several-killed-in-amazon-cargo-plane-crash-in-miami/a-79107365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least five people have died after a cargo plane crashed at Miami International Airport. The aircraft overran a runway, struck several vehicles and caught fire.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US envoys Witkoff and Kushner hold Ukraine talks after meeting Putin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db568c2736ae68dace514436b500366895400fb9a6fd12ae8e775b07c3f0684</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T22:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779--687b66a14041.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-envoys-witkoff-and-kushner-hold-ukraine-talks-after-meeting-putin/a-79054779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner held talks with Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Kyiv, seeking to revive efforts to end the war. But the latest diplomatic push seems to have produced no breakthrough.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt: Digesting the AfD's landmark election win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea3744d4b0d92916096e1092f540c14cd22a6feca65f066770781afb22f29085</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T21:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981--03f4036eaf84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-digesting-the-afd-s-landmark-election-win/a-79103981?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With well over 40% for the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD), Saxony-Anhalt has witnessed a landmark election night. DW's reporters were on the ground.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Election fraud claims spread in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66957e19fe1c2d50ced2350b8f3fc15cb4ee014521fae2d8b14a8f8a94b9e9ba</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T19:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254--984abe33c1c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-election-fraud-claims-spread-in-saxony-anhalt/a-79093254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">False and misleading claims are raising questions about the integrity of the election in Saxony-Anhalt. DW Fact Check takes a closer look.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany set to feel the impact of Saxony-Anhalt's AfD win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ca133f57184e47fabf2d9254645a10d543f35e557aea07dadc77855e4e577c1</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:20:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569--97dfb85b6e8e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-set-to-feel-the-impact-of-saxony-anhalt-s-afd-win/a-78874569?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The state election could have major consequences for Germany's government. Pollsters cite dissatisfaction with Merz as one reason for the CDU's poor showing.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Germany's postal voting system isn't rigged</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4c71468692fca48f92c1c3ba17281714a8a63112aaa7cdd6aa5723377e5202a7</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438--ffb06136be22.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-germany-s-postal-voting-system-isn-t-rigged/a-78958438?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of Germany's state elections in September, rumors began circulating on social media claiming that postal voting is not secure — claims that have also been made about other elections. Here's why they're wrong.</summary><category term="German election" /></entry><entry><title>Saxony-Anhalt election: Why the AfD is so strong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7df601728548cbed4a8170283b57456f277092e9a8bacfd84f542845a0caf522</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T18:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588--f7f12ed5af71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saxony-anhalt-election-why-the-afd-is-so-strong/a-78482588?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD has emerged as the strongest party in Germany's eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt by a wide margin. What is driving support for the far right in this predominantly rural eastern German state?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on Lebanon kill several despite truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb3fe946d85a6e6bbc08514d527fc69d84bc89958fa24a0c667051e75691536</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011--55ceb327e7e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-kill-several-despite-truce/a-79065011?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Lebanon's President Joseph Aoun has appealed to the international community to "take immediate action to stop these violations" of the ceasefire agreement between Israel and Lebanon.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Rahul Gandhi backs student protests in Maharashtra</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53c094f769e7cc466509d949fada0e570049059a57ebcbe8bee263cccf62a4fe</id><updated>2026-09-07T14:19:08Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T10:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198--c16d7d5783ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-rahul-gandhi-backs-student-protests-in-maharashtra/live-79043198?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Opposition Rahul Gandhi has said that students are "tormented" by the ruling Bharatiya Janata Party. The Congress politician has demanded immediate action into the demands of Maharashtra student protesters. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
